\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
For each compact smooth surface M without boundary and each smooth Riemannian metric g on M, is there a smooth map $F:M\to R^{4}$ with injective differential at every point and $F*\delta =g$? The map may have self-intersections, and M may be nonorientable.

\subsection{Short English statement}
For each compact smooth surface M without boundary and each smooth Riemannian metric g on M, is there a smooth map $F:M\to R^{4}$ with injective differential at every point and $F*\delta =g$? The map may have self-intersections, and M may be nonorientable.

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] Original question source or mathematical context.
\url{https://people.math.gatech.edu/~ghomi/Papers/op.pdf}.
\item[S2] OpenAI, manuscript citation page. Source of the formulation motivating this local problem.
\url{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/Smooth-isometric-immersions-of-closed-surfaces-into-Euclidean-four-space-September-23-2026/README.md}.
\end{itemize}

